<%# The curator's desk. Same head as the reader's pages plus the CSRF meta tag,
    which the queue's delete link needs: it is `data: { turbo_method: :delete }`,
    a JS-initiated request, and Turbo reads the token from the meta tag.

    This hangs off Admin::BaseController, not off a single controller, so the next
    thing added under /admin inherits it instead of quietly falling back to the
    reader layout and losing the tag. Nothing here is publicly cached. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
  </head>

  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
